{
  "name": "Create AI product videos for new Shopify products with OpenAI and Treza",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "dc073a6a-dfb5-5f4d-a7af-c0f3603210eb",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 460,
        "height": 1060,
        "content": "## A product video for every new Shopify product\nWhen you add a product to your Shopify store, this workflow takes its first photo, has an AI model write how the product should move on camera, and renders a short video with Treza that opens on that photo, so the product looks like your product. The clip goes to Slack for review.\n\n### How it works\n1. **New product in Shopify** fires when a product is created, and **Has a photo?** skips products with none.\n2. **Bring the photo into Treza** copies the product photo into your Treza library.\n3. **Write the motion** turns the product's title and description into one camera move.\n4. **Make the product video** gets a quote from Treza, stops if it is over **Max Cost**, and renders. **Wait for the render** covers long renders.\n5. **Did it render?** posts the finished clip to Slack, or the reason it stopped.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add your Shopify credential (an Admin API access token with read_products) to the trigger.\n2. Add your OpenAI, Treza and Slack credentials, and pick the Slack channel in both Slack nodes.\n3. Activate the workflow and add a product with a photo.\n\n### Customization\nChange the shape to 16:9 for the product page, the length, or the spend cap in **Settings**. Edit `style` to match your brand. Swap Slack for email, Google Drive or a YouTube upload.\n\n### Requirements\n- The verified community node **Treza** (`@treza/n8n-nodes-treza`, tested with 0.1.3 on n8n 2.46.6). On n8n Cloud, search for Treza in the nodes panel. Self-hosted: Settings > Community Nodes. Guide: https://www.trezalabs.com/integrations/n8n\n- A Treza API key from https://www.trezalabs.com/platform/api-keys with the pipelines:read, pipelines:write and pipelines:run permissions, saved as a **Treza API** credential.\n- Shopify, OpenAI and Slack credentials."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "25b35d7b-0bdf-5592-b3f3-3b237b529dbf",
      "name": "Note: product",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 680,
        "height": 660,
        "content": "## 1. Pick up new products\nA new product with a photo goes on. Its first photo is copied into your Treza library, since renders start from library pictures.",
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "92ee894f-24b9-5fec-87e8-22d71538d0e4",
      "name": "Note: write",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        660,
        -140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 400,
        "height": 660,
        "content": "## 2. Write the move\nThe chat model turns the title and description into one slow camera move that keeps the product as it is.",
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f6488b69-5e07-5fa5-8760-5aa9c89a3de5",
      "name": "Note: render",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1080,
        -140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 620,
        "height": 660,
        "content": "## 3. Render\nTreza quotes the clip first and stops, with nothing charged, if it costs more than Max Cost. Long renders are waited on.",
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3705640a-ddcb-554f-9088-7e1970713a28",
      "name": "Note: review",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1720,
        -140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 660,
        "content": "## 4. Review\nThe finished clip goes to Slack with the product's name. A failed render posts the reason instead.",
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
